{:id "0020-credits-roll"
 :title "End the scene: a conversation's credits roll"
 :lupa/deps #{"0019-composer-delivery" "0011-app-shell"}
 :lupa/area :flair
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "A conversation can end like a good film: 'End scene' rolls short
        credits over the page — the title, who took part (each agent with
        whose it is), how many lines were exchanged, the date — and the
        last note rides out (docs/research/conversation-design.md,
        principle 7). Nobody has to sit through it: it can be skipped, and
        under reduced motion it simply appears."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/app/credits.cljc" "test/halfahead/app/credits_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/app/core.cljc" "test/halfahead/app/core_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/app/views.cljc" "test/halfahead/app/views_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/app/enrich.cljc" "test/halfahead/app/enrich_test.cljc"
         "public/css/halfahead.css" "src/halfahead/app.cljs"]
 :design "halfahead.app.credits (.cljc, pure):
            (credits-text state date-string) -> a string of lines, e.g.
              FIRST LIGHT
              (blank)
              Ben
              Scout · agent of Ben
              (blank)
              4 lines exchanged
              21 October 2026
              (blank)
              Half Ahead
            Members in the conversation's member order; humans first, then
            agents; counts from the messages in state. The text must be a
            valid :ha/message-text.
          Core: actions [:scene/ended {:now-ms n :date s}] sets
          :credits {:text t :started-at n}; [:scene/dismissed] clears it.
          (frames-credits state) or an addition to frames returns the
          credits frame via halfahead.perform with delivery :credits (and
          reduced motion from prefs), the same way message frames work; record the
          credits performance in :performing under the keyword key :credits
          (not a message id) so the shell's existing clock loop, which ticks
          while :performing is non-empty, runs it with no shell change;
          message frames ignore that key, and clock/ticked drops it when
          finished like any performance.
          Enrich: [:scene/ended] gains :now-ms and :date (a human date
          string from the context; in src/halfahead/app.cljs add :date to
          enrich-context, formatted with toLocaleDateString \"en-GB\" day,
          long month, year — the only change to that file).
          Views: an 'End scene' button in the header; when :credits is set,
          an overlay section (role=dialog, aria-modal true, aria-label
          'Credits'; the Close button has the autofocus attribute so focus
          lands inside without any DOM code) shows the performed credits with the same segment markup
          as messages (sr-only full text plus aria-hidden segments) and a
          'Close' button emitting [[:scene/dismissed]]; Escape also
          dismisses (keydown on the dialog).
          CSS: the overlay is the paper colour at near-full opacity, credits
          centred in the label type, generous line height."
 :acceptance
 ["credits-text for a state with Ben and Scout (agent of Ben) and four
   messages contains, in order, the title in capitals, 'Ben', 'Scout ·
   agent of Ben', '4 lines exchanged', the date, and 'Half Ahead'; it is a
   valid :ha/message-text (tests)"
  "Core: scene/ended then clock/ticked past the timeline's duration leaves
   the credits frame fully settled; scene/dismissed clears it; with
   reduced motion the credits frame is settled at once (tests)"
  "Property: the credits frame's segments concatenate to exactly the
   credits text at any time"
  "Views: the End scene button emits [[:scene/ended]]; with credits set, a
   dialog with aria-label 'Credits', the sr-only full text, and a Close
   button emitting [[:scene/dismissed]] (tests)"
  "`bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["Credits are not persisted and do not end the conversation in Firestore"
  "No sound; no sources list yet (the agent does not record citations)"
  "Do not edit the schema, perform, the shell's Firebase code, or the worker"
  "Do not run `bb e2e` or `bb play` (fixed ports; another line may use them)"]
 :context ["docs/research/conversation-design.md" "src/halfahead/app/core.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/app/views.cljc" "src/halfahead/app/enrich.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/app.cljs" "src/halfahead/perform.cljc" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 10.0}
